-- title:
--   Smoothness over k of the two-chart model read off the charts
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a commutative ring, $F$ a field equipped with an $R$-algebra structure, and $j \in F$ a non-zero element. Write $\mathcal{O}_{\mathrm{fin}} =$ `chartAlgFin R F j` for the $R$-subalgebra of $F$ consisting of the elements of $F$ that are integral over the $R$-subalgebra generated by $j$, and $\mathcal{O}_{\mathrm{inf}} =$ `chartAlgInf R F j` for the elements integral over the $R$-subalgebra generated by $j^{-1}$; the scheme [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel R F j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236) is the pushout of the two maps $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the inclusions of these two subalgebras into the intermediate chart algebra, and `toBase R F j` is the morphism to $\operatorname{Spec} R$ induced by the two structure maps $R \to \mathcal{O}_{\mathrm{fin}}$, $R \to \mathcal{O}_{\mathrm{inf}}$. Let $k$ be a commutative $R$-algebra and $n$ a natural number. Assume that both $\operatorname{Spec}(k \otimes_R \mathcal{O}_{\mathrm{fin}}) \to \operatorname{Spec} k$ and $\operatorname{Spec}(k \otimes_R \mathcal{O}_{\mathrm{inf}}) \to \operatorname{Spec} k$, each given by $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the canonical map from $k$ into the tensor product, are smooth of relative dimension $n$. Then the second projection of the pullback of `toBase R F j` along $\operatorname{Spec}(k) \to \operatorname{Spec}(R)$, that is the base change $X \times_{\operatorname{Spec} R} \operatorname{Spec} k \to \operatorname{Spec} k$, is smooth of relative dimension $n$.
--
--   This is the glueing step for the two-chart integral model: smoothness of relative dimension $n$ of a fibre of the model over a base ring $k$ is checked on the two affine charts, whose base changes are the spectra of the two tensor products. It is used in establishing that Igusa's Kroneckerian model of the modular curve is smooth of relative dimension one in characteristic $p$.
-- source:
